      "id": 14,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "showLineNumbers": false
        },
        "content": "**Volume counts are physical.** Every replica of a volume counts, so with replication a collection shows a multiple of its logical volume count.\n\n**Growth panels** use `non_negative_difference` of the per-bucket maximum, so a bucket shows the bytes/files added inside it. Volumes are allocated in 30 GB chunks by default, which is why *Volumes per collection* moves in steps while *Stored bytes* grows smoothly.\n\n**Vacuum:** `Reclaimable bytes` above zero means deleted needles are still occupying disk \u2014 run `weed shell` \u2192 `volume.vacuum` during a quiet window.",
